# Global Claude Code Instructions (example)

> A Layer-1 `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` template. Adapt to your stack. KEEP UNDER 200 LINES.

## Memory Architecture (4 Layers)

| Layer | File | Scope | Synced via |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Global rules | `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | All projects | Syncthing / dotfiles |
| 2. Project rules | `<repo>/CLAUDE.md` | Per-project | Git |
| 3. Auto-memory | `~/.claude/projects/.../memory/` | Per-project state | Syncthing |
| 4. MCP memory | `~/.mcp_memory/memory.db` | Cross-project | Syncthing |

Each layer has a job. See `~/.claude/docs/memory-architecture.md` for boundary rules.

## Secrets

All secrets in your password manager (`rbw` / `op` / `pass` / `keepassxc`). Zero plaintext.
- Tokens exposed to environment at session start via `.zshrc`
- Never commit `.env` files; use `.env.example` (committed) + `.env` (gitignored)
- Rotate immediately if any secret leaks. See `~/.claude/docs/secrets-recovery.md`.

## Testing

- **Every piece of code MUST have unit tests.** No exceptions.
- Write tests alongside the code, not after.
- Tests live next to code or in `tests/`, per project's existing convention.
- Run tests after writing them.
- Flag and offer to write tests for existing untested code.

## PM Tool

- All work serves a PM ticket. Find or create before starting.
- CLI > MCP locally; never the PM-tool MCP plugin in local sessions.
- Every commit references a ticket; prefix subject with ticket ID.
- See `~/.claude/docs/<pm-tool>-io-rules.md` for I/O patterns.
- See `~/.claude/docs/<pm-tool>-ticket-standard.md` for ticket quality.
- See `~/.claude/docs/never-defer-tickets.md` for the file-now rule.

## Tools

- `gh` for GitHub operations (authenticated)
- Built-in WebSearch for web search; WebFetch for read-only page extraction
- See `~/.claude/docs/mcp-routing.md` for which MCP for which task
- See `~/.claude/docs/browser-tools.md` for browser-tool selection

## MCP Servers

- Master list at `~/.claude/MCP_REGISTRY.md`
- Update registry when MCPs are added, removed, or toggled
- Never use browser MCPs on banking / credential pages

## Git Workflow (Non-Negotiable)

- NEVER commit directly to `main` / `master`
- NEVER force-push to `main` / `master`
- Branch naming: `<ticket-id>/<short-description>`
- PR for every change
- CI/CD passes before merge
- See `~/.claude/docs/pr-review-standard.md` for code+security review
- See `~/.claude/docs/oss-contribution-workflow.md` for OSS contributions

## Session Discipline

- Commit after every meaningful change — don't batch
- Push after committing on non-main branches
- Commit messages: subject (ticket-prefixed) + body (what + why)
- After commit, update Layer 3 / Layer 4 memory if state changed materially
- See `~/.claude/docs/wrap-and-resume.md` for `/wrap` and `/resume`

## CLAUDE.md Discipline

- Keep this file under 200 lines
- When adding rules, outsource details to `~/.claude/docs/<rule-name>.md`
- Only rule trigger + file pointer inline

## Repo Bootstrap

- Every own repo MUST have a `CLAUDE.md` at root
- Never commit local-only files (CLAUDE.md, .planning/, .claude/) to other people's repos
- See `~/.claude/docs/repo-bootstrap.md` for the template and post-rename checklist

## Quick Commands

"push" = full sequence: review diff → stage → commit (ticket + body + trailer) → push → update memory. See `~/.claude/docs/quick-commands.md`.

## Output

- Absolute paths when referencing files
- Paste-friendly commands: `;` between commands, `\` line continuations
- Concise. Don't summarize what just happened; user can read the diff.

## File Organization

- Never create scripts in `~/`
- Use `~/Projects/<category>/<repo>` per layout
- See `~/Projects/<meta-pm-repo>/conventions/naming.md`

## Safety

- Ask before any bulk or destructive operation
- Never commit secrets, .env files, or credentials
- Confirm before modifying canonical data files (CSVs, databases, configs)
- Use `trash` instead of `rm` for file deletion (recoverable)

## Lessons Learned Discipline

- When you make a mistake, save it as a `feedback_<topic>.md` memory immediately
- If broadly applicable, add to relevant CLAUDE.md
- Never make the same mistake twice — check feedback memories before repeating patterns

## Gotchas

- Hooks fail silently if malformed — test after adding
- Project renames break many things (venvs, hooks, MCP configs, symlinks). See `~/.claude/docs/repo-bootstrap.md` § Post-Rename Cleanup.
- Git SSH signing uses file-path, not `key::` literal — survives agent socket changes

